    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1103">

                <pb facs="1074" n="908" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg908"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/20495½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Funston to the
                            Adjutant General of the Army
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fort Sam Houston</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 6, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4509. Following received from General Pershing from Columbus dated February 5:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Expeditionary forces returning from Mexico crossed the line to-day, last
                            troops leaving Mexico at 3 p.m. Transportation pertaining to expedition
                            was sufficient to bring out all Government property. Am leaving
                            to-morrow Roon for El Paso. General Swift will supervise movement of
                            remaining troops ordered to new stations.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>As soon as General Swift has completed duty referred to he will proceed to El
                    Paso to command cavalry division.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Funston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
